# The committed vector bytes, frozen.
#
# emit/build.py refuses to write a vector whose bytes differ from this file, and
# refuses to drop or add one. The corpus's manifest, its projections and its
# accepted encodings are CLAIMS ABOUT these bytes and are expected to change as
# more runtimes are asked; the bytes themselves are what every consumer has
# already pinned, so changing one silently is the one edit this directory must
# not be able to make by accident.
#
# Sealed 2026-09-20, after the first two consumers (poc/python, poc/cpp) had run
# against them. Re-seal deliberately with `python3 emit/build.py --reseal`, which
# is a decision and not a step.
#
